# ci/module-aliases.stock515 - stock 5.4 module name -> what 5.15 calls it
#
# The stock /vendor/lib/modules/modules.load is a 5.4 list.  Several entries
# were renamed between 5.4 and 5.15, so a plain name comparison reports them as
# missing when the driver is in fact present.  Each mapping below is a measured
# rename, not a guess: the left side was read from the device's own modules.load
# over adb, the right side comes from the 5.15 tree's KO_MODULE_NAME.
#
# Format:  <stock name>:<our name>
# A value of "-" means "no 5.15 module; handled another way", with the reason.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mali_kbase -> mali_kbase
#   NOT a rename after all, and this entry exists to record why.  An earlier
#   alias mapped mali_kbase to mali_gondul on the belief that 5.15 renamed the
#   GPU driver.  It did not.  The board's GPU is the *natt* driver, not gondul:
#   the live device tree says soc/mm/gpu@23100000 compatible = "sprd,mali-natt",
#   and gpu/sprd/natt/platform/qogirl6 matches both the SoC (qogirl6) and the
#   driver.  Built with CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME=qogirl6, natt produces
#   mali_kbase.ko -- byte-for-byte the name the stock loader asks for.  The
#   alias was therefore chasing a driver we do not ship.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# omnivision_td4160 -> omnivision_tcm-modules
#   NOT a guess about the touch panel.  The 5.4 device loads five touch modules
#   at once (adaptive_ts, focaltech_ft8722, focaltech_ft8756_spi_ts,
#   nvt_nt36xxx_spi_ts, omnivision_td4160) because the stock ROM ships every
#   driver it has and lets probe-fail sort it out, so "it is loaded" says
#   nothing about which one bound.  The device tree is what answers it: the only
#   enabled touch node is spi@20150000/transsion-touchscreen@0, and the chip on
#   it is an Omnivision TD4160.  kernel5.15/touchscreen/odm/omnivision_tcm
#   declares td4160 in its source and is what the vendor's own ums9230
#   EXT_MODULES list builds, so that is the 5.15 provider of the same function.
#   The other four are alternative panels, not this board.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# agdsp_access -> (no separate module; folded into snd-soc-sprd-card)
#   Recorded because it LOOKS like a gap and is not, and the reason is not
#   visible from the file list alone.  Our SC2730 codec calls agdsp_access_enable
#   from ten call sites, and agdsp_access.ko is in neither our build nor the
#   vendor's 5.15 EXT_MODULES list -- which reads like a module we failed to
#   build.  It is not: `llvm-nm -u` on the built codec shows no undefined agdsp
#   symbol, because snd-soc-sprd-card.ko (which we do build, and which the codec
#   depends on) exports agdsp_access_enable.  The vendor's list carries
#   audio/sprd_audio/agdsp_pd and nothing else agdsp-shaped, so on 5.15 the
#   access path lives in the card driver.  A DT node existing
#   (soc/agcp/agdsp-access) is therefore not evidence of a missing module.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# sprd-top-dvfs -> (genuinely absent from this 5.15 tree; NOT fixed here)
#   Left unaliased on purpose so it keeps being reported.  The node
#   aon/topdvfsctrl@64014000 declares compatibles sprd,qogirl6-topdvfs-dev,
#   sprd,topdvfs-dev and syscon, and no driver in this tree binds any of them;
#   nothing parses its device-dcdc-cells children (dcdc-mm, dcdc-modem) either.
#   The top_dvfs_clk in drivers/clk/sprd/ums9230-clk.c is a clock of that name,
#   not the device, which is an easy false match.  Unlike the entries above this
#   one is a real functional hole -- MM/modem DCDC voltage control -- and it
#   would need a new regulator driver, not a config line.  Flagged, not fixed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
misc_sprd_uid:sprd_uid
sprd_gpu_cooling:sprd_thermal_ctl
gnss_common_ctl_all:unisoc_gnss_common_ctl_all
omnivision_td4160:omnivision_tcm-modules
wcn_bsp:wcn_bsp
